sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant TD as TeardownCommand
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant SSM as AWS SSM

    Note over User,SSM: baas admin teardown -- needs the elevated BaasCliDeployerPolicy.<br/>Deletes the CORE stack only. The CI stack and the MongoDB cluster are untouched.
    User->>TD: baas admin teardown [--stack-name] [--yes] [--delete-bucket]
    Note over TD: ConfigService.load() from ~/.baas/config.yaml<br/>stack = --stack-name, else aws.coreStackName from config

    rect rgb(255, 235, 235)
        Note over TD,EC2: Gate 1 -- never tear down under a live run
        TD->>EC2: describeInstances(tag baas-role=benchmark-runner, state=running)
        EC2-->>TD: instance IDs
        alt running runner instances found
            TD-->>User: abort, list the instance IDs, exit 1
        end
    end

    opt --yes not set
        Note over TD,User: Gate 2 -- explicit confirmation
        TD->>User: prompt: type the stack name to confirm deletion
        User-->>TD: typed input
        alt input does not match the stack name exactly
            TD-->>User: "Aborted." exit 0
        end
    end

    alt --delete-bucket set
        TD->>S3: listObjectsV2Paginator(bucket)
        S3-->>TD: object keys (paginated)
        TD->>S3: deleteObject(key) for each object
        TD->>S3: deleteBucket(bucket)
        alt deletion fails
            Note over TD: warn and CONTINUE -- leaving the stack behind is worse<br/>than leaving the bucket behind, and the bucket is recoverable by hand
        end
    else default (bucket retained)
        Note over TD,S3: the bucket survives -- DeletionPolicy Retain means CloudFormation<br/>will not remove it either
    end

    TD->>CF: deleteStack(stackName)
    CF-->>TD: delete accepted
    TD->>CF: waiter.waitUntilStackDeleteComplete()
    loop poll DescribeStacks
        CF-->>TD: status = DELETE_IN_PROGRESS
    end
    CF-->>TD: status = DELETE_COMPLETE

    TD->>SSM: deleteParameter(/PREFIX/mongo/connection-string)
    Note over SSM: ParameterNotFoundException is<br/>silently swallowed if absent
    SSM-->>TD: deleted (or not found, ignored)

    opt bucket was retained
        TD-->>User: warn: `baas admin setup` as this identity will FAIL while the bucket<br/>exists -- its name is a hash of your caller ARN, so the next setup asks<br/>for the same name. Delete it by hand or re-run with --delete-bucket.
    end
    TD-->>User: "MongoDB cluster NOT touched (connect-only)" and exit 0
